1
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:03,671
[wind howling]

2
00:00:06,214 --> 00:00:08,216
It is pointless to be afraid.

3
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:09,426
[Coco gasps]

4
00:00:09,718 --> 00:00:11,553
[EASTHIES]
Once your memories of magic

5
00:00:11,595 --> 00:00:12,721
have taken their leave of you,

6
00:00:12,763 --> 00:00:15,390
so too will your feelings
of fear.

7
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:18,185
You will be an Outsider
and nothing more.

8
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:20,437
Why won't you listen to us?

9
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:22,481
We've told you,
it's not what you think!

10
00:00:22,523 --> 00:00:25,567
Please, no. You can't!

11
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:32,825
[gasps]

12
00:00:33,701 --> 00:00:36,954
[both gasping, screaming]

13
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:44,545
What's this?

14
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:46,171
The Serpent's Bed of Sand?

15
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:49,132
They're trying to explain
the situation to you!

16
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:51,510
The least you can do
is hear them out!

17
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:53,428
Who are they?

18
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:55,430
Children, sir.

19
00:00:55,848 --> 00:00:58,392
They burned the pennants.

20
00:00:59,727 --> 00:01:02,270
Typical adults.
You say "children,"

21
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:05,941
as though children are things
instead of human beings.

22
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:07,568
I hate that.

23
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:10,153
[EASTHIES] The circumstances
are irrelevant.

24
00:01:10,863 --> 00:01:13,782
The law has been broken.

25
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:17,202
Peace and order
are vital to the world,

26
00:01:17,244 --> 00:01:19,162
and if we are to maintain
that peace,

27
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:22,416
witches must honor the law
with strict adherence.

28
00:01:22,958 --> 00:01:25,586
A single crack,
and the wall collapses.

29
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:27,170
As such,

30
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,590
exceptions cannot be allowed.

31
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:32,009
[QIFREY]
So very talkative, Easthies,

32
00:01:32,051 --> 00:01:34,344
and so determined not to listen.

33
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:40,642
Do show my apprentices
some respect, won't you?

34
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:43,228
Of course.

35
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:45,272
These girls are your students.

36
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:48,817
And every bit as insolent
as their master.

37
00:01:48,859 --> 00:01:51,570
[chuckles] If it means
they're unlike you,

38
00:01:51,612 --> 00:01:53,530
then I welcome their insolence.

39
00:01:54,782 --> 00:01:58,077
Especially if this is how
the Knights Moralis operate.

40
00:01:59,954 --> 00:02:02,831
Our desire is only
to preserve order.

41
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:08,003
To alter the terrain itself,
as occurred in the Dadah Range

42
00:02:08,045 --> 00:02:09,922
or the Shadow Forest
of Thristas...

43
00:02:09,964 --> 00:02:12,173
Such is the power
of the spells of war

44
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:13,968
used before the pact.

45
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:18,346
Daring to invoke magic
of this nature

46
00:02:18,388 --> 00:02:21,516
is an act that demands
to be dealt with.

47
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:23,351
[QIFREY] Don't you want
to find out what happened

48
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:26,480
before you start
erasing memories?

49
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:28,065
You should know.

50
00:02:28,107 --> 00:02:29,733
My apprentices
are hardly equipped

51
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:31,526
for a spell of this scale.

52
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:34,113
I've not given them the tools
nor the technique.

53
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:36,782
Presuming you did not,

54
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:39,158
is it possible
the Brimmed Caps did?

55
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,452
[Qifrey gasps]

56
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:46,667
[OLRUGGIO] Oi, you two!

57
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:49,252
Amidst this
rousing debate of yours,

58
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:52,589
I fear it may have escaped you
what a witch's purpose is.

59
00:02:52,631 --> 00:02:55,884
To spread the blessings
of magic to all.

60
00:02:55,926 --> 00:02:57,845
Ringing any bells for you?

61
00:02:57,886 --> 00:03:00,347
Thankfully, these girls
remember, at least.

62
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:04,476
So don't just float there.
Make yourselves useful!

63
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:07,855
Those lovely pennants look like
they could do some good!

64
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:10,189
[horse neighs]

65
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:17,322
Thank you.
Is this going to heal him?

66
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:20,034
No, but it's stopped
the bleeding.

67
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:22,077
And now I shall take him
to Kalhn.

68
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:25,122
With a doctor's care,
he may be able to reco--

69
00:03:25,164 --> 00:03:26,414
[DAGDA] I saw you.

70
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:29,793
You used your magic
to repair your pennants!

71
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:33,047
Surely it can repair
his wounds, too!

72
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:36,925
Magic has to be capable
of such things!

73
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:39,761
[LULUCI]
I'm sorry, but it is not.

74
00:03:39,803 --> 00:03:42,056
[breathes shakily] You lie!

75
00:03:42,097 --> 00:03:43,348
I don't believe you!

76
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:44,850
[LULUCI] Unhand me.

77
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:51,272
Now, shall I take the boy
with me or leave him here?

78
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:53,232
[Dagda cries softly]

79
00:03:56,153 --> 00:03:57,404
[DAGDA] Take him.

80
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:01,240
And please, keep him safe.

81
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:03,952
[horse neighs]

82
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:05,370
[EASTHIES]
Let us seal off the site.

83
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:07,581
For now, only witches
may be present.

84
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:10,542
Once the Outsiders are gone...

85
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:14,462
we'll resume questioning
our witnesses.

86
00:04:16,255 --> 00:04:17,925
[Coco grunts uneasily]

87
00:04:19,218 --> 00:04:21,636
[♪ opening theme song playing]

88
00:05:57,732 --> 00:06:00,319
A basic spell. Unremarkable.

89
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:04,405
Plainly not the level of power
needed for such destruction.

90
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:05,699
Indeed not.

91
00:06:07,826 --> 00:06:09,244
Your hands, girl.

92
00:06:09,286 --> 00:06:10,537
[COCO] Huh?

93
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,706
In some cases,

94
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:14,499
the Brimmed Caps
tattoo their bodies

95
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:16,417
with grotesque seals.

96
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:19,171
The seals of forbidden spells,

97
00:06:19,213 --> 00:06:20,588
to alter the physical form

98
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,966
or enhance the power
of their magic.

99
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:29,639
Hands covered in ink stains,
and a beginner's calluses.

100
00:06:29,681 --> 00:06:31,266
[Easthies exhales softly]

101
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,940
That's quite enough.

102
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:40,441
[Easthies sighs]

103
00:06:43,278 --> 00:06:45,530
I shall report these events
to the Great Hall

104
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:48,116
and open a full investigation
in due course.

105
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:51,953
If your atelier is found
to be the source of the problem,

106
00:06:51,995 --> 00:06:53,538
I'll show no mercy.

107
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:56,333
I suggest you take care
not to lose

108
00:06:56,375 --> 00:06:58,752
that which you've
only begun to learn.

109
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:06,343
[Qifrey sighs]

110
00:07:07,094 --> 00:07:09,263
That was a close one,
wasn't it?

111
00:07:09,304 --> 00:07:11,598
I'm glad we all made it
through unscathed.

112
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:13,308
[Tetia chuckles]

113
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:18,230
[QIFREY] Perhaps it was unwise
to have split everyone up.

114
00:07:18,272 --> 00:07:19,731
I apologize!

115
00:07:19,773 --> 00:07:22,317
You aren't to blame
for this, Master!

116
00:07:22,359 --> 00:07:25,820
- Everyone showed up just...
- [QIFREY] However, Agott, Coco.

117
00:07:27,281 --> 00:07:28,990
You need to know
that what you did

118
00:07:29,032 --> 00:07:30,449
was extremely dangerous.

119
00:07:31,076 --> 00:07:33,870
If the secrets of magic
had been revealed here today,

120
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:36,915
every one of the people
we saved

121
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:39,376
would have had
their memories erased.

122
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,045
Our memories make us
who we are,

123
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:44,839
and you very nearly
took that away from them.

124
00:07:45,548 --> 00:07:47,092
Sorry, Master.

125
00:07:47,134 --> 00:07:48,760
So am I.

126
00:07:49,677 --> 00:07:50,762
[AGOTT] That's that.

127
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:54,224
I doubt I'll take that test
any time soon.

128
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:56,893
But in the end,
you got through it.

129
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:58,519
Therefore...

130
00:07:58,728 --> 00:08:00,605
I'll make the arrangements
for you

131
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:02,565
to take the second test, Agott.

132
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:03,608
[Agott gasps softly]

133
00:08:04,318 --> 00:08:06,778
If you pass,
you will officially be qualified

134
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,905
to accompany me on outside work.

135
00:08:08,947 --> 00:08:10,365
[Agott exclaims]

136
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:12,242
Can you promise
you won't use magic

137
00:08:12,284 --> 00:08:14,119
in front of people before then?

138
00:08:14,161 --> 00:08:15,494
[AGOTT] Uh?

139
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:17,038
Yes!

140
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,333
[TETIA] Aw! Only Agott?

141
00:08:19,374 --> 00:08:22,002
Not fair!
What about the rest of us?

142
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:24,545
I seem to recall that
you three still need to complete

143
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:26,423
the Basics
of Casting Primer first.

144
00:08:26,465 --> 00:08:27,506
No!

145
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:28,549
That's fine.

146
00:08:28,591 --> 00:08:30,593
I despise taking tests anyway.

147
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:33,180
You mean there are
more tests to come?

148
00:08:33,763 --> 00:08:36,016
- [OLRUGGIO] Are you certain?
- [QIFREY] Huh?

149
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:39,978
As I recall, you feared Agott
was getting ahead of herself.

150
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,146
True.

151
00:08:41,188 --> 00:08:43,231
- [QIFREY] But...
- You can do it, Agott!

152
00:08:44,274 --> 00:08:46,109
[QIFREY]
...this feels different.

153
00:08:47,194 --> 00:08:49,029
And in all fairness,

154
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:51,198
I believe she's earned
a bit of trust.

155
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:53,074
[OLRUGGIO] You spoil them.

156
00:08:53,116 --> 00:08:54,284
[QIFREY] How can I not,

157
00:08:54,326 --> 00:08:56,453
when they're always
so hard on themselves?

158
00:08:56,495 --> 00:08:57,662
[OLRUGGIO] Hmm.

159
00:08:57,704 --> 00:08:59,122
[AGOTT] Master Qifrey!

160
00:08:59,164 --> 00:09:01,916
I want to get back
and start practicing!

161
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:03,626
Not quite yet.

162
00:09:04,169 --> 00:09:05,504
[AGOTT] Uh...

163
00:09:09,383 --> 00:09:12,551
There's one more thing
we still need to do.

164
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:16,181
[UTOWIN] That girl was
Qifrey's new apprentice, right?

165
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:18,517
If the rumors
going around are true.

166
00:09:20,018 --> 00:09:22,729
Do you have any evidence
to suggest that they are?

167
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:26,191
No. Bit hard to recover
anything of note

168
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:27,984
from a petrified house.

169
00:09:29,069 --> 00:09:32,113
Very well. Then we'll have
to extract a confession.

170
00:09:32,155 --> 00:09:33,281
Look...

171
00:09:34,241 --> 00:09:38,078
That spell dried up the entirety
of the downriver area.

172
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:41,580
A single fallen rock
can bring down the bank,

173
00:09:41,622 --> 00:09:42,665
divert the river,

174
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:44,959
and alter
the environment beyond.

175
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:46,503
Were that to happen,

176
00:09:46,545 --> 00:09:48,838
much of the scenery
would be lost.

177
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:51,007
Never to be restored.

178
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:56,637
That girl may well be
such a rock.

179
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,639
She cannot be allowed to fall.

180
00:09:58,681 --> 00:10:01,518
I must pluck her out
delicately.

181
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:04,062
[Coco exclaims]

182
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,316
[QIFREY]
Olruggio has a special pen.

183
00:10:08,775 --> 00:10:10,651
It's called a Searwire Wand,

184
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:12,404
and it lets him burn
Casting Seals

185
00:10:12,446 --> 00:10:14,281
into rocks and trees.

186
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,742
[OLRUGGIO]
This should help for now.

187
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,718
[QIFREY]
The river has begun to return.

188
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:39,055
The effects of the rending spell
must be wearing off!

189
00:10:40,557 --> 00:10:41,682
Hm?

190
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:47,147
- Coco.
- [COCO] Uh?

191
00:10:50,942 --> 00:10:51,943
[COCO] Huh?

192
00:10:51,985 --> 00:10:53,612
[QIFREY] Here,
you dropped these.

193
00:10:53,652 --> 00:10:54,613
[COCO] Oh.

194
00:10:54,653 --> 00:10:56,072
[QIFREY] Do take care.

195
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:59,242
Your cap and ink aren't items
you want to leave behind.

196
00:11:01,244 --> 00:11:02,745
[COCO] I'm sorry.

197
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:04,872
Thank you, Master Qifrey.

198
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,043
Wait, what? That's strange.

199
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,378
[QIFREY] Huh?

200
00:11:11,296 --> 00:11:14,090
[COCO] The vial
is still completely full.

201
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:15,342
[Coco gasps]

202
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:18,011
A magic vial
that refills itself?

203
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:20,096
What an amazing world this is!

204
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:23,016
[QIFREY] Coco, do you mind
if I take a look at that?

205
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:25,435
All right.

206
00:11:26,353 --> 00:11:28,271
[Qifrey breathes shakily]

207
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:41,700
[WITCH] Magic is a falsehood
that makes this world vibrant.

208
00:11:42,701 --> 00:11:45,872
These hands draw
the most beautiful of spells...

209
00:11:46,456 --> 00:11:50,043
Only to be so hideously
stained with ink!

210
00:11:51,752 --> 00:11:53,712
Yet no lie...

211
00:11:55,507 --> 00:11:58,051
can survive close scrutiny.

212
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:01,638
Hm.

213
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:10,938
I wonder how long
this ruse can be maintained.

214
00:12:15,235 --> 00:12:17,070
How very curious.

215
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:20,198
This is the ink you were given
by Nolnoa in Kalhn?

216
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,449
Yes?

217
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:23,493
[QIFREY] Hm.

218
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:26,954
[COCO] Uh...

219
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,707
- Wow!
- Olruggio...

220
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:30,250
the girls should head home.

221
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:31,626
Could you escort them there?

222
00:12:31,668 --> 00:12:34,962
What? Some other business
to attend to?

223
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:37,048
- [QIFREY] Well...
- [COCO] Uh...

224
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:39,842
It occurs to me
that young Coco here

225
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:42,053
still hasn't obtained her pen.

226
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:45,139
Kalhn is close,
so we'll make a stop on the way.

227
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,642
Say, could you
pick me up some wine?

228
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:50,478
One bottle first flush,
one bottle aged!

229
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:52,146
Aye. That'd be grand.

230
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:54,815
- I'm sorry.
- [COCO] Huh?

231
00:12:57,151 --> 00:13:00,154
[QIFREY] There's something
I really need to look into.

232
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:10,457
Hold on, wasn't the door here?

233
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:12,667
Oh, dear me.

234
00:13:12,709 --> 00:13:15,044
It appears they're closed
for today.

235
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:17,171
[COCO] What? You mean
the whole shop goes away

236
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:18,548
when they're not open?

237
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:23,219
Oh! Hello, Mr. Qifrey.

238
00:13:23,261 --> 00:13:24,471
[Coco gasps]

239
00:13:24,512 --> 00:13:26,473
And you're that girl
from before.

240
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:29,643
Hello, Tartah!
What good luck.

241
00:13:29,684 --> 00:13:31,478
I need to speak
with Mr. Nolnoa.

242
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:34,063
Ah, sorry, one moment.

243
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:53,750
There we are. Go right in.

244
00:13:58,296 --> 00:13:59,631
[Coco gasps]

245
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:03,092
It's nothing like
last time I was here!

246
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:06,680
Different doorknobs
lead to different rooms.

247
00:14:06,721 --> 00:14:08,473
What else would you expect?

248
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:11,017
Granda should be up
on the third floor.

249
00:14:11,058 --> 00:14:13,852
Thank you. Please excuse us.

250
00:14:14,312 --> 00:14:15,938
[TARTAH] Oh, uh...

251
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:19,066
- Before you go...
- [COCO] Huh?

252
00:14:19,108 --> 00:14:21,569
I don't know your name.

253
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:24,739
Then I'll tell you!
My name is Coco!

254
00:14:24,781 --> 00:14:27,534
Coco, your leg's
all scratched up,

255
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:29,076
you really ought to clean it.

256
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,286
[COCO] Oh...

257
00:14:30,328 --> 00:14:31,746
[TARTAH] Come with me.

258
00:14:31,788 --> 00:14:34,415
I can disinfect it
with tranquileaf.

259
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:36,751
[footsteps]

260
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:46,511
[COCO]
So many unfamiliar components!

261
00:14:47,679 --> 00:14:49,597
[Coco gasps softly]

262
00:14:51,182 --> 00:14:52,350
Oh, wow!

263
00:14:53,059 --> 00:14:55,562
What are these glittery powders?

264
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:57,522
Please, just leave it.

265
00:14:57,564 --> 00:15:00,483
I have those
specially arranged.

266
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:02,360
- [Coco exclaims]
- They're magical dyes.

267
00:15:02,402 --> 00:15:04,987
If you mix them into the ink,
you can alter its effects.

268
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:06,740
[footsteps]

269
00:15:08,949 --> 00:15:10,243
[QIFREY] Mr. Nolnoa...

270
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,161
Why, Qifrey.

271
00:15:12,203 --> 00:15:14,288
Don't you know
we're closed today?

272
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:17,083
Yes. Apologies.

273
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,586
Only teasing.

274
00:15:19,627 --> 00:15:22,756
Good to see you.
And I know why you're here.

275
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:25,592
You're wondering
about the Casting Seal

276
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:27,385
on those paving tiles,
aren't you?

277
00:15:27,427 --> 00:15:28,636
[Qifrey gasps softly]

278
00:15:28,678 --> 00:15:31,138
[NOLNOA] I still
haven't figured it out yet.

279
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:34,642
I tried using a spell
to separate out the magic dyes.

280
00:15:35,184 --> 00:15:38,396
But they're blended together
quite thoroughly, I fear.

281
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:41,357
Have you managed to find
any clues on your end?

282
00:15:41,399 --> 00:15:44,819
Perhaps. I have
something interesting here.

283
00:15:46,654 --> 00:15:48,489
[Nolnoa exclaims] Oh-ho!

284
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:51,992
Hmm.

285
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:58,541
Hmm.

286
00:15:58,957 --> 00:16:00,627
It looks very similar!

287
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:05,005
In fact, I'd say that
faint blue hue is identical!

288
00:16:05,924 --> 00:16:08,593
Qifrey, tell me.
Where on earth did you...

289
00:16:10,261 --> 00:16:12,430
What's going on?

290
00:16:12,472 --> 00:16:14,766
Isn't this one of my vials?

291
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:17,518
[QIFREY] That day...

292
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:21,856
The Brimmed Caps must have cast
some kind of spell on the vial.

293
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:25,735
Qifrey, no!

294
00:16:25,777 --> 00:16:28,237
You shouldn't risk
drawing with that ink

295
00:16:28,279 --> 00:16:29,614
until I analyze it.

296
00:16:30,657 --> 00:16:32,074
Qifrey!

297
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:36,746
Oh! What's that one
with the color

298
00:16:36,788 --> 00:16:38,414
that looks like aquamarine?

299
00:16:38,957 --> 00:16:41,375
In the big container
hanging from the ceiling!

300
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:44,086
Right, that would be
azuremoon flower.

301
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:47,005
Adding it to the ink
makes your spells last longer.

302
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:52,136
[COCO] And what about
the little sparkly white one,

303
00:16:52,178 --> 00:16:54,096
on the shelf
right across from it?

304
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:56,808
Blushing bride butterfly scales.

305
00:16:56,850 --> 00:16:59,560
Mixing those in
will turn the ink invisible,

306
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,729
concealing the lines
of the casting seal.

307
00:17:01,771 --> 00:17:03,189
And next to that?

308
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:06,484
Well, the narrow bottle
is powdered roaming scallop,

309
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:07,861
and the squat, round one

310
00:17:07,902 --> 00:17:10,655
is powdered golden blaze
wyrm scale.

311
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:16,828
You're amazing!

312
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:18,997
You're just amazing, Tartah!

313
00:17:19,037 --> 00:17:20,999
I can't believe you memorized
all those names

314
00:17:21,039 --> 00:17:22,959
and can rattle them off
just like that!

315
00:17:23,001 --> 00:17:24,711
It is our job to sell them.

316
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:26,504
You're so lucky...

317
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:28,631
Living in a magic stationer's!

318
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:30,090
Just look at this room,

319
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:32,426
at all of these bottles,
and all these shelves!

320
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:34,303
It's crazy! [exclaims]

321
00:17:34,345 --> 00:17:37,015
Living here must be the best!

322
00:17:37,055 --> 00:17:38,140
[Tartah sighs]

323
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:41,435
I'd say living in
an atelier's much better.

324
00:17:41,853 --> 00:17:43,103
You say a lot of things

325
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:45,356
that are strange to hear
from a witch.

326
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:48,150
I thought you were
an apprentice witch too,

327
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,235
are you not?

328
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:51,445
[TARTAH] Well, I'm...

329
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:53,113
[Tartah breathes uneasily]

330
00:17:54,032 --> 00:17:55,157
[COCO] Oh, wow.

331
00:17:55,533 --> 00:17:58,076
That red powder's so bright,
can you tell me what it does?

332
00:17:58,118 --> 00:17:59,412
[TARTAH] Which one?

333
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,080
Up there! On the shelf!

334
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:04,000
[TARTAH] Hm?

335
00:18:07,003 --> 00:18:08,254
- Right between...
- Hey!

336
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:10,214
...the rusty brown one
and the aquamarine!

337
00:18:10,256 --> 00:18:13,342
Can you just tell me
where it is on the shelf?

338
00:18:16,094 --> 00:18:19,139
It's the bright red one,
you see it, right?

339
00:18:20,558 --> 00:18:21,935
[Coco gasps]

340
00:18:21,976 --> 00:18:23,811
[bottles rattling]

341
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:29,191
[TARTAH]
Where'd that light come from?

342
00:18:31,151 --> 00:18:33,195
That was pretty scary!

343
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:35,281
- You all right?
- [Tartah gasps softly]

344
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:41,955
None got broken!
That's a relief, isn't it?

345
00:18:43,664 --> 00:18:45,792
- Huh?
- [TARTAH] This is terrible.

346
00:18:47,710 --> 00:18:49,670
A total disaster!

347
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:51,839
The labels came off.

348
00:18:51,881 --> 00:18:53,716
And they're all mixed up.

349
00:18:54,092 --> 00:18:56,886
Granda told me so clearly
not to touch them,

350
00:18:56,928 --> 00:18:58,721
and now it's a great big mess.

351
00:18:58,763 --> 00:19:00,056
Don't worry!

352
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,433
I'll help you put them back
in their proper places!

353
00:19:02,475 --> 00:19:05,311
Let's start with these.
What are they?

354
00:19:06,729 --> 00:19:08,773
Just tell me which color
goes with which and--

355
00:19:08,815 --> 00:19:10,316
I have no idea!

356
00:19:11,484 --> 00:19:13,653
What? But earlier, you...

357
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:16,656
I remember them
by their position on the shelf.

358
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:19,199
I can't tell the colors apart!

359
00:19:20,743 --> 00:19:22,078
[Coco gasps softly]

360
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:28,126
Please...

361
00:19:28,668 --> 00:19:30,252
Just get out of here.

362
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:31,921
But I...

363
00:19:34,172 --> 00:19:35,675
[TARTAH] I'm sorry.

364
00:19:36,801 --> 00:19:39,971
I know you want to help,
but I'm afraid you can't.

365
00:19:40,513 --> 00:19:41,597
There are certain things

366
00:19:41,639 --> 00:19:43,975
that certain people
just can't do.

367
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:47,103
These Silverwash eyes
of mine mean that

368
00:19:47,145 --> 00:19:48,771
no matter how hard I study,

369
00:19:48,813 --> 00:19:50,606
I'll never become a witch.

370
00:19:55,193 --> 00:19:57,905
You can't say I didn't warn you!

371
00:19:58,781 --> 00:20:00,950
Qifrey? You all right there?

372
00:20:00,992 --> 00:20:02,200
[Qifrey grunts]

373
00:20:03,703 --> 00:20:05,121
Qifrey!

374
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:10,626
For a Casting Seal that small
to have so great an impact...

375
00:20:10,668 --> 00:20:11,961
[Qifrey grunts]

376
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:16,049
I think we're dealing
with a twinned bottle spell.

377
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:20,386
Two different vessels,
sharing contents.

378
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:21,721
There should be a small medal

379
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:24,557
inscribed with
a Casting Seal in the fluid.

380
00:20:25,307 --> 00:20:27,518
They made Coco use this.

381
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:30,604
And when she did,
the ink was replaced

382
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:32,481
with some mysterious substance.

383
00:20:33,024 --> 00:20:36,527
This bottle
is connected to them.

384
00:20:38,236 --> 00:20:39,488
Finally...

385
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:42,366
I have what I need!

386
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,827
What do you mean?

387
00:20:44,869 --> 00:20:48,246
You're saying that ink
can unleash power like that,

388
00:20:48,288 --> 00:20:50,958
even from small,
scribbled seals?

389
00:20:51,542 --> 00:20:53,127
It can't be!

390
00:20:53,169 --> 00:20:54,921
No, it mustn't be!

391
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:58,674
This... This is far beyond
my capacity!

392
00:20:58,716 --> 00:21:00,760
I must inform
the Great Hall, of course!

393
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:02,220
You can't!

394
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:05,181
It's imperative that this not go
to the Knights Moralis,

395
00:21:05,223 --> 00:21:06,933
nor to the Great Hall.

396
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:10,603
It's best if no one becomes
aware of what we've discovered.

397
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:12,772
Why, Qifrey?

398
00:21:14,065 --> 00:21:16,150
What are you suggesting?

399
00:21:17,151 --> 00:21:18,318
You...

400
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,821
Do you truly understand
the implications

401
00:21:20,863 --> 00:21:22,698
of what you're saying?

402
00:21:23,490 --> 00:21:25,034
What is it, then?

403
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:28,579
What is it you mean to do
with that ink?

404
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:33,251
Mr. Nolnoa, forgive me.

405
00:21:42,468 --> 00:21:44,178
- [QIFREY] Coco.
- [COCO] Uh?

406
00:21:45,221 --> 00:21:46,889
Sorry for the wait.

407
00:21:46,931 --> 00:21:49,225
Now, about that ink of yours...

408
00:21:49,976 --> 00:21:51,852
It seems he accidentally
gave you

409
00:21:51,894 --> 00:21:53,479
something very expensive.

410
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:57,108
I bought you a bag
to make up for it. Enjoy.

411
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:58,525
Oh!

412
00:21:58,692 --> 00:22:00,694
I love it, thank you!

413
00:22:02,947 --> 00:22:04,657
[Coco chuckles]

414
00:22:05,783 --> 00:22:08,410
[♪ closing theme song playing]

415
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:16,127
Master...

416
00:22:17,044 --> 00:22:19,880
Can you tell me
what "Silverwash" means?

417
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:22,549
[QIFREY] Silverwash syndrome.

418
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:24,760
A congenital condition
of the eye

419
00:22:24,802 --> 00:22:26,512
that causes
those who suffer from it

420
00:22:26,553 --> 00:22:29,098
to see the entire world
in silver.

421
00:22:30,390 --> 00:22:31,642
I imagine it would cause

422
00:22:31,684 --> 00:22:33,936
particular difficulty
for witches,

423
00:22:33,978 --> 00:22:36,522
given how crucial
their eyesight is.

424
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:37,982
And unfortunately,

425
00:22:38,024 --> 00:22:40,026
witches can be
rather unaccommodating

426
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:41,443
of differences.

427
00:22:44,155 --> 00:22:45,363
Coco.

428
00:22:47,825 --> 00:22:50,328
There's no need
to look so concerned.

429
00:22:50,368 --> 00:22:52,163
You'll be fine.

430
00:22:52,997 --> 00:22:55,749
As long as you're a student
at my atelier,

431
00:22:55,791 --> 00:22:58,002
you'll have me to protect you.

432
00:22:58,544 --> 00:23:00,546
You have nothing
to worry about.

433
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:01,755
I assure you.

434
00:23:03,049 --> 00:23:05,092
Not a thing.

435
00:23:06,552 --> 00:23:07,845
[TARTAH] Uh?

436
00:23:08,304 --> 00:23:11,015
Granda, I'm sorry.

437
00:23:11,057 --> 00:23:13,684
That light earlier startled me,

438
00:23:13,726 --> 00:23:15,686
and all the jars
got knocked down.

439
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:19,523
Was that light caused by
a spell or something?

440
00:23:19,815 --> 00:23:21,650
One of Mr. Qifrey's?

441
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:26,072
[NOLNOA] What, now? A light?

442
00:23:28,157 --> 00:23:30,659
I don't recall any such thing.

443
00:23:32,078 --> 00:23:33,453
Granda?

